   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT directing the department of transportation to study the weight\nlimitations for fire vehicles with pneumatic tires",
    "basePrintNo": "S7829",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7829-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 3,
       "fullName": "Thomas Croci",
       "imgName": "893_thomas_croci.jpg",
       "incumbent": false,
       "memberId": 893,
       "sessionMemberId": 955,
       "sessionYear": 2017,
       "shortName": "CROCI"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7829\n\nSPONSOR: BOYLE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act directing the department of transportation to\nstudy the weight limitations for fire vehicles with pneumatic tires\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill will require the department of transportation to study whether\nthe current weight exemptions for fire trucks are adequate.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Requires department to conduct a study within 3 months of the\neffective date.\n\n2. Requires the study to be completed within 1 year of the study begin-\nning, and be reported to the governor and the legislature.\n\n3. Department should evaluate the data with the assistance of experts in\nhighway and road limitations, fire vehicles and traffic safety.\n\n4. Effective Date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAlthough section 385 subsection 17-b provides an exemption for fire\ntrucks, these heavy fire trucks often exceed the maximum weight under\nthis exemption. Currently fire trucks that exceed the weight limit\nallowed through section 17-b may receive a permit from DOT to legally\ntravel on the State and local highway system.\n\nThis legislation would require DOT to evaluate whether the weight\nrestriction exemption should be raised for fire trucks. It is important\nto ensure all vehicles traveling using the state and local highway\nsystem are traveling at safe and appropriate weights.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
